<p id="mwTg">Since <i id="mwTw">X</i> is a compact oriented manifold, <i id="mwUA">X</i> has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundamental_class" title="Fundamental class" id="mwUQ">fundamental class</a>, and so <i id="mwUg">X</i> can be integrated over.</p>

<p id="mwUw">Let <i id="mwVA">Z</i> be a complex submanifold of <i id="mwVQ">X</i> of dimension <i id="mwVg">k</i>, and let <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt25" id="mwVw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"i\\colon Z\\to X"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle i\colon Z\to X}">
  <semantics>
