    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle (p,q)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9769c58523b9b639866a2d48e657d9c26911143a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:5.082ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (p,q)}"/></span>.  We can integrate <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt28" id="mwWw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\alpha"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle \alpha }">
