  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/91bba876e952ac507077670c9d1d46a0d451df3e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:15.479ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle z=(z_{1},\ldots ,z_{k})}"/></span>.  The inclusion of <i id="mwZQ">Z</i> in <i id="mwZg">X</i> means that we can choose a local <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basis_(linear_algebra)" title="Basis (linear algebra)" id="mwZw">basis</a> on <i id="mwaA">X</i> and have <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt32" id="mwaQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"z_{k+1} = \\cdots = z_n = 0"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle z_{k+1}=\cdots =z_{n}=0}">
