    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle N^{c}H^{k}(X,\mathbf {Z} )=H^{k}(X,\mathbf {Z} )\cap (H^{k-c,c}(X)\oplus \cdots \oplus H^{c,k-c}(X)).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/036f6410e2992fff8b3b77f534df96929dffa417" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:59.19ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle N^{c}H^{k}(X,\mathbf {Z} )=H^{k}(X,\mathbf {Z} )\cap (H^{k-c,c}(X)\oplus \cdots \oplus H^{c,k-c}(X)).}"/></span></dd></dl></dd></dl>
<p id="mwAV8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFGrothendieck1969" about="#mwt99" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwAWA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvtxt","href":"./Template:Harvtxt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Grothendieck"},"2":{"wt":"1969"}},"i":0}}]}'>Grothendieck (1969)</a> observed that this cannot be true, even with rational coefficients, because the right-hand side is not always a Hodge structure.  His corrected form of the Hodge conjecture is:</p>

<dl id="mwAWE"><dd id="mwAWI"><dl id="mwAWM"><dd id="mwAWQ"><b id="mwAWU">Generalized Hodge conjecture.</b>  <i id="mwAWY">N</i><span style="padding-left:0.12em;" about="#mwt100" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"i sup","href":"./Template:I_sup"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;c&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><sup><i>c</i></sup></span><i id="mwAWg">H</i><span style="padding-left:0.12em;" about="#mwt101" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"i sup","href":"./Template:I_sup"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;k&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><sup><i>k</i></sup></span>(<i id="mwAWo">X</i>, <b id="mwAWs">Q</b>) is the largest sub-Hodge structure of <i id="mwAWw">H</i><span style="padding-left:0.12em;" about="#mwt102" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAW0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"i sup","href":"./Template:I_sup"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;k&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><sup><i>k</i></sup></span>(<i id="mwAW4">X</i>, <b id="mwAW8">Q</b>) contained in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt103" id="mwAXA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{k-c,c}(X) \\oplus\\cdots\\oplus H^{c,k-c}(X)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mathjax_ignore" alttext="{\displaystyle H^{k-c,c}(X)\oplus \cdots \oplus H^{c,k-c}(X).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mi>c</mi>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mi>c</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>⊕<!-- ⊕ --></mo>
        <mo>⋯<!-- ⋯ --></mo>
        <mo>⊕<!-- ⊕ --></mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>c</mi>
            <mo>,</mo>
            <mi>k</mi>
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mi>c</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{k-c,c}(X)\oplus \cdots \oplus H^{c,k-c}(X).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a5bf46c5120a16027536dcf4c9297fbfe1c8fb68" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:29.333ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{k-c,c}(X)\oplus \cdots \oplus H^{c,k-c}(X).}"/></span></dd></dl></dd></dl>
<p id="mwAXE">This version is open.</p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwAXI" aria-labelledby="Algebraicity_of_Hodge_loci"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Algebraicity_of_Hodge_loci">Algebraicity of Hodge loci</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hodge_conjecture&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Algebraicity of Hodge loci"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAXM">The strongest evidence in favor of the Hodge conjecture is the algebraicity result of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFCattaniDeligneKaplan1995" about="#mwt104" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwAXQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Harvtxt","href":"./Template:Harvtxt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Cattani"},"2":{"wt":"Deligne"},"3":{"wt":"Kaplan"},"4":{"wt":"1995"}},"i":0}}]}'>Cattani, Deligne <span typeof="mw:Entity">&amp;</span> Kaplan (1995)</a>.  Suppose that we vary the complex structure of <i id="mwAXU">X</i> over a simply connected base.  Then the topological cohomology of <i id="mwAXY">X</i> does not change, but the Hodge decomposition does change.  It is known that if the Hodge conjecture is true, then the locus of all points on the base where the cohomology of a fiber is a Hodge class is in fact an algebraic subset, that is, it is cut out by polynomial equations.  Cattani, Deligne &amp; Kaplan (1995) proved that this is always true, without assuming the Hodge conjecture.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwAXc" aria-labelledby="See_also"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="See_also">See also</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hodge_conjecture&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: See also"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwAXg"><li id="mwAXk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tate_conjecture" title="Tate conjecture" id="mwAXo">Tate conjecture</a></li>
<li id="mwAXs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hodge_theory" title="Hodge theory" id="mwAXw">Hodge theory</a></li>
<li id="mwAX0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hodge_structure" title="Hodge structure" id="mwAX4">Hodge structure</a></li>
